{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Allow all public sector employees to stand as local councillors",
        "additional_details": "We are requesting the Government to remove barriers preventing public sector employees from standing and serving as local councillors once elected. Teachers, further education staff, and workers in essential services such as water, fire, and ambulance services dedicate their lives to their Local Authority and supporting communities. We believe that allowing them to contribute through local government would strengthen democracy, improve representation, and bring valuable experience into local decision-making.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to review Section 80 of the Local Government Act 1972 so eligibility rules reflect modern working lives. We believe public servants shouldn't be prevented from standing for local election as clear guidance & proportionate safeguards can protect democracy & public confidence",
